*** File formats supported by release 0.2b3 ***

format	summary
--------------------------------------------------------------------
BMP	Reads and writes 1, 4, 8 and 24-bit uncompressed images. RLE
        compressed files are not supported.  OS/2 core and info
	versions are supported, though.

CUR	Reads and writes 4 and 8-bit Windows cursor files.  If a file
	contains multiple cursors, the largest size is loaded.  Ani-
	mated cursors are not supported.

DCX	Reads DCX files (compound PCX files).  See PCX for details.
	You can use seek/tell to load individual frames.

EPS	Identifies EPS images.  Writes "L", "RGB" and "CMYK" images.
	Output is an EPS file covering (0, 0, xsize, ysize) in the
	Postscript coordinate space.  Use scale/translate operators
	to put the image in place.  (For easy printing, use the PSDraw
	interface).

FLI	Identifies Autodesk FLI and FLC animations.

GBR	Reads GIMP brushes.

GD	Reads GD images through the "GdImageFile" module.  Note that
	this format cannot be automatically identified by Image.open(),
	so you have to use the GdImageFile.open() function instead.

GIF	Reads GIF87 and GIF89 images.

ICO	Reads and writes 4 and 8-bit Windows icon files.  If a file
	contains multiple icons, the largest size is loaded.

IM	Reads simple versions of the IFUNC/LabEye IM format.  Only
	writes greyscale images (mode "L").

IMT	Reads single-layer, 8-bit images of this Image Tools format.

JPEG	Reads and writes "L", "RGB" and "CMYK" images [1]

MNG	Reads a small subset of the MNG animation/metafile
	format.  This driver is experimental. [2]

MPEG	Identifies MPEG video streams.

MSP	Identifies MSP images.

PCD	Reads PhotoCD (PCD) images.  PIL reads the base resolution
	only (768x512).

PCX	Reads 1, 4, 8, and 24-bit compressed images.  Uncompressed PCX
        files are not supported (not that it's very likely that anyone
        should stumble upon such a file).

PDF	Identifies and writes PDF images. [3]

PNG	Identifies and reads W3O PNG files of all possible flavours
	with the exception of interlaced files [2]

PPM	Reads and writes "1", "L", and "RGB" images.

PSD	Identifies Adobe PSD files.

SGI	Reads uncompressed "L" and "RGB" images.

SUN	Reads uncompressed "1", "L" and "RGB" images.

TGA	Reads uncompressed 24 and 32-bit "RGB" images.

TIFF	Reads and writes "1", "L", "RGB" and "CMYK" images.  PIL reads
	striped or tiled images, uncompressed, or JPEG, LZW or PackBits
	encoded.  The TIFF tag directory can be inspected through the
	"tag" member.  Multi-image files can be handled though the
	"seek/tell" methods.  PIL currently writes uncompressed, single
	strip images only.

WMF	Reads and renders a subset of the Windows metafile format.
	This driver is experimental.

XBM	Reads and writes XBM bitmaps.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes:

[1] When linked with the IJG JPEG library (version 6.0).  Otherwise, PIL
    only knows how to identify JPEG files.

[2] When linked with the ZLIB library (version 1.0).  Otherwise, PIL only
    knows how to identify (and verify) PNG/MNG files.  Note that LIBPNG
    is not used to read PNG files.

[3] Acrobat complains on files generated by the current version, but still
    renders them correctly.
